nd it  allowed me to discover and to share lots  of cool stuff so for instance I joined  the time series forecasting competition  to learn about methods like arima or  tools like profit and this particular  example was about predicting web views  for specific International Wikipedia  pages  so here in this example plot you see  that the views for the Wiki page of the  band 21 Pilots exploded dramatically in  early 2016. I don't really know them I  don't know why that happened but there  are some there's some interesting lag  effects here as to how this rise  happened in the different countries that  are coded by different colors and some  interesting lags and these spikes too  that pop up right so features like this  made this competition interesting and  challenging  and I also joined my first NLP  competitions learning how to use Julius  and David's great tidy tax package and  in this particular one I was flexing my  storytelling muscles and I wrote my own  chilling short story around the analysis  of language used by classic horror  writers like Shelley or Lovecraft right  so you see that Love and Death are there  at the center of most of these stories  intertwined in an eternal battle  and with every new notebook and every  new competition I was learning something  new new tools new tricks and new ideas  from meeting other people's notebooks  and exchanging Thoughts with them you  see one of the great things about kaggle  notebooks is that you can fork and tweak  them directly on the website using this  little button up there and you see this  often with competition modeling code  when people build on each other's models  and make them better step by step  the kaggle community is very good at  learning from each other and it's  standing on each other's shoulders to  see further than we otherwise could  and myself I owe a lot to the support of  the carrier Community which made me the  very first notebook's Grandmaster  which is a title that you can earn  through 